{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794233772,"nonce":"QYXpeQD4R6CB/NKPPqjbDCBss8o=","title":"L3 — Crate lint table with a curated pedantic subset","message":"## Context\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[lints]` table; clippy runs default-only. `-W clippy::pedantic` reports ~150 warnings, mostly noise (separators, `must_use`, `# Errors` docs), but a few are worth enforcing.\n\n## Files\n- `Cargo.toml` — add `[lints.rust]` / `[lints.clippy]`\n- Hits today: `needless_pass_by_value` / `large_types_passed_by_value` (`src/app.rs:1450`, `:1477`, `:1833`), `redundant_closure` (`src/writes.rs:26`, `:37`, `:50`), `unchecked_time_subtraction` (`src/ui/tooltip.rs:473`, `:491`, tests), lossy `f32`/`usize` casts in `src/ui/`\n\n## Approach\n- Enable as `warn`: `redundant_clone`, `needless_pass_by_value`, `large_types_passed_by_value`, `redundant_closure_for_method_calls`, `cast_possible_truncation`, `cast_sign_loss`, `cast_precision_loss`, `unchecked_time_subtraction`, `implicit_clone`, `needless_collect`; `rust.unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`.\n- Fix the hits; where a cast is intentional (UI layout math), use `#[expect(clippy::..., reason = \"...\")]` at the narrowest scope, never `#[allow]`.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Blanket `clippy::pedantic`; `too_many_lines` on `App::update` (epic follow-up).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `Cargo.toml` carries the lint table\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes with it\n- No new `#[allow(...)]` attributes; every suppression is `#[expect]` with a `reason`","files":null}]}